{
  "id": "diviners-sage",
  "term": "diviner’s sage",
  "definition": "Diviner’s sage is a hallucinogenic plant, Salvia divinorum, traditionally used in ritual ceremonies and known for producing salvinorin A. In psychology-related contexts, it may be discussed because salvinorin A has powerful dissociative effects and acts on the kappa-opioid receptor, which is involved in pain, mood, memory, learning, and emotional control.",
